From 59c248445e17ce14e1527d34da46b2139ec384f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:43:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Dissipative heating: return the KE removed by explicit
 diffusion and damping as heat (option, default off)

config_dissipative_heating = 1 heats each layer by the kinetic energy that
u_dissipation_3d, w_dissipation_3d, 3-d divergence damping and the absorbing
layer's w damping remove there (first-order work u*d(rho u)*volume), once per
step after the microphysics, at constant volume. Edge work is halo-exchanged
and split between the edge's two cells, so runs reproduce across
decompositions. Diffusion also moves kinetic energy, so this local heating
has either sign.

config_dissipative_heating = 2 heats with positive-definite dissipation rates
in summation-by-parts form (rho*nu*(D^2 + zeta^2) for del2, rho*nu4*
(f*(grad D)^2 + (grad zeta)^2) for del4, the symmetric flux form for w del2),
each rescaled per step so that its reproducing domain sum equals the term's
work; the domain heat is option 1's. Default 0: bit-identical.
